# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, Git checks the repository out with CRLF on Windows. Biome
# formats with LF, so every line of every file reads as changed and the format
# check fails on the Windows CI job while passing everywhere else.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree on all platforms, which is also what
# the shell scripts and the shebang in dist/index.js need in order to run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish files Git should never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
